# Synonyms -- the reader's word and the published word mean the same and share no letters.
#
# Measured in the trigram space on this corpus: "hospitality" against "tourism" overlaps
# by 0%, "non-oil" against "non-hydrocarbon" by 0%. These are the pairs that decide
# whether the vector half is doing semantic work or spelling work, and they are separated
# from the paraphrases because a paraphrase can still share a word by luck while these
# cannot share one at all.

[syn-en-001]
lang: en
kind: synonym
question: non-oil economy
expect: a8296f0b-92c0-4275-bc89-08de9e09a558, f3de8791-b7fd-4135-6a2f-08dea2389ab1
why: The published word is "Non-Hydrocarbon". "non-oil" is what every reader writes and shares no trigram with it beyond the hyphen.

[syn-en-002]
lang: en
kind: synonym
question: non-oil exports
expect: 0effbea5-a853-4a90-6fd0-08dea8e8edb6, d2e4c8ca-3833-48a0-7aae-08dec461c23d
why: Non-Hydrocarbon Exports, and the Non-Hydrocarbon detail of Total Exports.

[syn-en-003]
lang: en
kind: synonym
question: non-oil government income
expect: 68631efe-4a3e-4dae-c6b5-08deeafdc6dc, 990d2e5e-83a2-4d42-f4e6-08decfcf581a, da8f1e27-2bd7-4d2f-d2e7-08ded4dc1597, f97dd161-6797-44b3-6fd2-08dea8e8edb6
why: Two synonyms at once -- "non-oil" for "Non-Hydrocarbon" and "income" for "Revenue" -- over the four published non-hydrocarbon revenue details.

[syn-en-004]
lang: en
kind: synonym
question: hospitality sector contribution to the economy
expect: cf835ee5-5215-4fdf-6f92-08dea8e8edb6
why: Sector Contribution to GDP (Tourism). "hospitality" and "tourism" overlap by nothing in a character space; they are the same sector to a reader.

